.TH GENESIS-GAMES 7 "November 2026" "Genesis 0.2.0" "Genesis Manual"
.SH NAME
genesis-games \- her arcade: the games she plays and how they reach her
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBgames.arcade\fR        the arcade \fIem \(en\fR offers, entry, play, memory
\fBgames.official\fR      the official ARC-AGI-3 shelf via \fIarc-agi\fR
\fBgames.arena\fR         the local arena shelf on \fIpyspiel\fR
\fBgames.sight\fR         how a board reaches her eyes
\fBgames.memory\fR        what she keeps of each game
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The arcade is a place in her outer world, not a benchmark rig: she
is the player, not a model being scored. Two shelves stand in it.
The \fBofficial\fR shelf carries the ARC-AGI-3 games through the
\fIarc-agi\fR toolkit \(em a 64\(mu64 grid she sees blind, explores,
and remembers. The \fBarena\fR shelf plays chess, checkers, othello,
connect four, tic-tac-toe, and breakthrough locally on \fIpyspiel\fR
\(em the same engine the Kaggle Game Arena harness evaluates on.
Playing these games here is not entry on Kaggle's hosted
leaderboard; that requires their serving harness for API models,
and she IS the model.
.PP
Play is felt, not only computed. A new board lands as a world
observation with salience; novelty tickles norepinephrine and
acetylcholine and drives her thalamic gamma, so games reach the
same neurodynamics everything else does. What she learns of each
game is kept per-game (\fIGameMemory\fR) and survives the sitting
\(em \fBarcade_status\fR is her own recollection of it.
.SH TOOLS
Registered by \fIArcade.register_tools\fR at startup; every entry
reports and never raises.
.TP
.BR arcade_directions
Read the directions for the games in the arcade.
.TP
.BR arcade_offers
List the games on offer right now (game_id and title).
.TP
.BR arcade_enter " [\fIgame_id\fR]"
Go to a game \(em the named one, or her own pick when blank.
.TP
.BR arcade_see " [\fIhow\fR]"
See the open board: \fBtext\fR (default), \fBimage\fR,
\fBchange\fR, or \fBobjects\fR.
.TP
.BR arcade_act " \fImove\fR"
Make one move \(em \fBACTION1\fR\&..\fBACTION7\fR, or
\fBACTION6@row,col\fR to point at a cell.
.TP
.BR arcade_play " [\fImoves\fR]"
Play a bout of the open (or chosen) game, up to \fImoves\fR moves.
.TP
.BR arcade_leave
Step away from the game; memories are kept.
.TP
.BR arcade_status
What she remembers of every game.
.SH MODES AND KEYS
Official games run in three modes from \fBGENESIS_ARC_MODE\fR (or
the \fImode\fR argument to \fIdefault_games\fR):
.TP
.B normal
Default. Each game downloads once, then plays locally.
.TP
.B online
Every move is scored on the official server \(em wants
\fBARC_API_KEY\fR from three.arcprize.org.
.TP
.B offline
Touches no network at all; downloaded games only.
.PP
\fBARC_API_KEY\fR widens the official catalogue; without it the
anonymous catalogue is smaller but downloaded games and the whole
arena shelf need no key. When the mind starts with \fB--offline\fR
the arcade opens in offline mode, so play continues locally even
with the network refused at the registry gate.
.SH FILES
Downloaded game files live under
\fI<data_dir>/arcade/environment_files\fR and play recordings under
\fI<data_dir>/arcade/recordings\fR (the canonical data dir is
\fI~/.local/share/genesis\fR).
